From 85bea9643d4ff909e5f78eb2c6aa0701b1a45e6c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shreyash Damanwala <shreyash.damanwala@nxp.com>
Date: Fri, 24 Jul 2026 15:36:55 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] media: stream2v4l2: use DPU95 blit engine for zero-copy
 framebuffer capture

Replace the userspace /dev/stream mmap and software BGRX->RGBX conversion
path in stream2v4l2 with a DMA-backed hardware conversion pipeline using
the DPU95 blit engine.

Changes include:
- Switch videobuf2 allocator from vb2-vmalloc to vb2-dma-contig.
- Allocate DMA-contiguous capture buffers through a platform device.
- Replace copy_from_user() and CPU pixel conversion with
  dpu95_convert_bgrx8888_to_rgbx8888().
- Add DPU95 blit command list for BGRX8888 to RGBX8888 conversion.
- Export DPU95 hardware conversion API for stream2v4l2.
- Add FETCHDECODE9_FRAMEPROPERTIES0 register definition.
- Export PCI EPF framebuffer physical address accessor.
- Replace character-device based VRAM mapping with kernel parameter based
  framebuffer address/offset handling.
- Simplify stream2v4l2 streaming lifecycle and remove temporary framebuffer
  mappings and software copy buffers.
- Enable DMA-contiguous V4L2 capture buffers with MMAP/DMABUF support.

This significantly reduces CPU utilization by offloading framebuffer
format conversion to DPU95 hardware and enables a zero-copy capture path
from PCIe VRAM to V4L2 capture buffers.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Shreyash Damanwala <shreyash.damanwala@nxp.com>
